.Dd October 21, 2026
.Dt SEATD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm seatd
.Nd mediate access to workstation graphics and input devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl n Ar fd
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Op Fl l Ar level
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the upstream seat management daemon, built into HalfBSD.
It runs in the foreground and grants connected libseat clients controlled
access to graphics, input devices and virtual terminals.
The Lua workstation graph supervises it as a required service.
Clients must have permission to connect to
.Pa /var/run/seatd.sock .
HalfBSD starts the daemon with root ownership and group
.Ql video ;
add workstation users to that group explicitly and establish a new login session
for supplementary group changes to take effect.
.Pp
The flags are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h
Print usage.
.It Fl v
Print the upstream version.
.It Fl n Ar fd
Write a newline to the supplied descriptor and close it when ready.
.It Fl u Ar user
Set the socket owner.
.It Fl g Ar group
Set the socket group.
.It Fl l Ar level
Set logging to debug, info, error or silent.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width LIBSEAT_BACKEND
.It Ev LIBSEAT_BACKEND
Clients may explicitly select
.Ql seatd .
.It Ev SEATD_SOCK
Override the socket path for libseat clients.
.It Ev SEATD_VTBOUND
Set to 0 only for isolated tests that must not acquire a virtual terminal.
Do not disable terminal binding for ordinary desktop operation.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/seatd.sock
.It Pa /var/run/seatd.sock
Local seat management socket.
.It Pa /usr/include/libseat.h
Client API declarations and contracts.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halfinit 8 ,
.Xr halfsvc 8
.Sh SECURITY
Socket access permits privileged graphics/input operations.
Do not grant access to all users or make the socket world writable.
Do not run a second daemon over the same socket or launch a compositor as root.
.Sh HISTORY
HalfBSD imports seatd and libseat 0.9.3 from the upstream MIT-licensed project.
